528 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"patch_8\"><path d=\"M 46.1 139.04 L 392.06 139.04 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"text_13\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(87.731675 27.962759) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-3d\" d=\"M 1184 2573 L 1670 2573 Q 2125 2573 2352 2784 Q 2579 2995 2579 3315 L 2579 3360 Q 2579 3712 2358 3888 Q 2138 4064 1779 4064 Q 1434 4064 1216 3913 Q 998 3763 858 3507 L 461 3814 Q 576 3994 749 4160 Q 922 4326 1178 4435 Q 1434 4544 1792 4544 Q 2170 4544 2477 4413 Q 2784 4282 2966 4032 Q 3149 3782 3149 3418 Q 3149 2989 2899 2726 Q 2650 2464 2291 2374 L 2291 2349 Q 2534 2304 2748 2166 Q 2963 2029 3097 1795 Q 3232 1562 3232 1222 Q 3232 838 3043 547 Q 2854 256 2512 89 Q 2170 -77 1715 -77 Q 1331 -77 1059 35 Q 787 147 598 320 Q 410 493 269 685 L 672 992 Q 845 730 1072 566 Q 1299 403 1709 403 Q 2182 403 2425 620 Q 2669 838 2669 1229 L 2669 1280 Q 2669 1677 2425 1891 Q 2182 2106 1709 2106 L 1184 2106 L 1184 2573 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3d\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_14\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(170.497225 38.012966) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-42\" d=\"M 1920 -77 Q 1414 -77 1068 92 Q 723 262 547 556 Q 371 851 371 1216 Q 371 1670 620 1942 Q 870 2214 1274 2323 L 1274 2374 Q 922 2496 714 2768 Q 506 3040 506 3424 Q 506 3936 880 4240 Q 1254 4544 1920 4544 Q 2586 4544 2960 4240 Q 3334 3936 3334 3424 Q 3334 3040 3126 2768 Q 2918 2496 2566 2374 L 2566 2323 Q 2970 2214 3219 1942 Q 3469 1670 3469 1216 Q 3469 851 3293 556 Q 3117 262 2774 92 Q 2432 -77 1920 -77 z\nM 1920 390 Q 2387 390 2643 601 Q 2899 813 2899 1190 L 2899 1325 Q 2899 1702 2643 1913 Q 2387 2125 1920 2125 Q 1453 2125 1197 1913 Q 941 1702 941 1325 L 941 1190 Q 941 813 1197 601 Q 1453 390 1920 390 z\nM 1920 2573 Q 2336 2573 2557 2755 Q 2778 2938 2778 3277 L 2778 3373 Q 2778 3712 2557 3894 Q 2336 4077 1920 4077 Q 1504 4077 1283 3894 Q 1062 3712 1062 3373 L 1062 3277 Q 1062 2938 1283 2755 Q 1504 2573 1920 2573 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-42\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_15\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(253.262775 32.987862) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" d=\"M 2912 0 L 2400 0 L 2400 877 L 243 877 L 243 1350 L 2112 4467 L 2912 4467 L 2912 1325 L 3558 1325 L 3558 877 L 2912 877 L 2912 0 z\nM 2368 4051 L 749 1325 L 2400 1325 L 2400 4051 L 2368 4051 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3c\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_16\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(336.028325 15.4) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3f\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p6bf9a96d73\"><rect x=\"46.1\" y=\"11.528\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Trays per hour by step","note":null},"answer":"<p>Cooking is the bottleneck at 118 trays an hour: 377.6k trays, <b>362.5k good</b>, against demand of 440k.</p> <p>Packing is already the fastest step (145/hour). Making it faster changes nothing: output stays at 362.5k. <b>Zero extra meals.</b></p> <p><b>So-what:</b> the robot can only be justified on labour savings, not on growth.</p>"},{"q":"Alternatives: an extra kettle to make cooking 18% faster ($180k), and a second blast-freezer to add 15% freezing capacity ($220k). Evaluate.","exhibit":{"kind":"table","headers":["Option","Cost ($k)","Bottleneck after","Good trays (k)","Extra contribution ($k/yr)"],"rows":[["Packing robot","600","Cook","362.5","0"],["Faster cooking","180","Blast freeze","380.9","74"],["Faster cooking + second freezer","400","Prep","399.4","147"]],"title":"Exhibit 2 · Options compared","note":null,"align":["l","r","r","r","r"],"boldLast":false},"answer":"<p><b>Cooking only:</b> 139/hour, but the blast freezer (124/hour) becomes the bottleneck: 380.9k good trays, +18.4k, $74k a year, payback 2.4 years.</p> <p><b>Cooking and freezer:</b> both are now above 130/hour, so <b>prep becomes the bottleneck</b>: 399.4k good trays, +36.9k, $147k a year for $400k: payback <b>2.7 years</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> this line is nearly balanced, so each fix only moves the limit to the next step. Even with both, Glacier is 40.6k trays short. Prep is manual, so the cheap next step is an extra prep worker per shift (to 150/hour). Cooking is then the limit again at about 427.7k good trays; the last 12.3k need around 90 hours of weekend overtime a year.</p>"},{"q":"The operations director says the robot also saves four packers' wages. How do you handle that?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Fair point: it's a cost-saving project, not a growth project, and should be judged on its own payback (four packers' wages vs $600k). It may still be worth doing later. But growth depends on cooking, freezing and prep, so those come first.</p>"}],"reco":"Don't buy the packing robot to grow: packing isn't the bottleneck, so it adds no meals. Instead add a kettle and a second blast-freezer: output rises from 362.5k to 399.4k good trays, adding about $147k a year and paying back in 2.7 years. Prep then becomes the limit: an extra prep worker per shift takes output to about 427.7k, and weekend overtime covers the rest. Evaluate the robot separately as a labour-saving project. Risk: freezer temperature compliance can't be compromised for speed. Next step: confirm the freezer supplier's lead time.","great":["Rejects the proposal with numbers, not opinion","Sees the line is nearly balanced: each fix moves the bottleneck to the next step","Separates growth projects from cost projects","Handles the director's objection respectfully"],"id":49,"slug":"glacier-meals"}